WHY GPLv3, AND NOT A CHOICE

Blend X-Ray links against blender-asset-tracer, which is GPLv2-or-later. A
work built on and linking against a GPL library must be distributed under
GPL-compatible terms, and GPLv2-or-later permits redistribution under GPLv3.
So the licence is inherited from a dependency rather than picked. README.md
says so at more length, under "Licence -- why GPLv3 and not MIT".

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The source tree contains no third-party code. The published Windows
executable, however, is a single-file PyInstaller build that packs the Python
interpreter, Tcl/Tk and several libraries inside it; their licences and
copyright notices ship beside it as THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, and the source
of that file is bundle/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt in this repository.

